Z||000005||JSocha||11-24-2001||09:09 PM||||I don't know about you guys.  But I tried to get into the Christmas spirit today, since it is the weekend  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> by displaying my Tanabaums  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> in the bedroom with the wife but she didn't seem at all impressed with my decorations.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||9
Z||000006||rodmcneill||11-24-2001||09:31 PM||||Spray paint any spiders gold and sprinkle sparklies on them while the paint is still wet. Quite pretty really, especially the big ones.||||reg||12
Z||000007||deceler8||11-25-2001||11:35 AM||||String lights on all the parts cars you have, especially if they're up on blocks in the front yard.<P>And use the chaser light strings on the wheels, giving the impression the cars are moving.<P>Seriously, a guy down the street usually puts up a 6 by 10 foot sign with lights saying "Happy Holidays from the &gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;" family...it's so tacky that every year I dream of re-wiring it to say something like...<P>"Bah Humbug"<BR>"Happy Holidays from the neighborhood pedophile"<BR>"Telemarketers...Come and get it"<BR>"I love it up the assss"<P>"Osama wuz here"||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cheever3000||11-25-2001||08:55 PM||||Best thing I've seen was pretty simple, but just makes you sit & stare.  The guy had several tall trees in his front yard, and of course the leaves had fallen by this time of year.  He dropped 10 or so white chaser lights straight down from the high branches, and left some solid white lights laying around the ground where those strands came down.  At night in the dark, it looked like snow or white rain, slowly falling into little pools.  It was beautiful.  This was in Waynesville Ohio.  I keep saying I'm going to do that someday.<P><BR>||||reg||3
