Z||000012||ChopTop||11-26-2001||11:05 AM||||I put Christmas lights on my dogs and set them in the front yard.<P>It's a good thing.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Ken Wittlief||11-26-2001||11:25 AM||||my favorite decoration is dark blue christmas lights everywhere - looks awesome at night - esp when there is snow all around<BR> <BR> just have to worry about you house being mistaken for a runway by passing jetliners :c)<P> putting lights around a garden edge where they wont get stepped on looks super when covered with snow - the snow lights up and glows.<P> something else I like is when someone puts floodlights under trees, pointing straight up, so the branches lite up at night - looks mysterious.||||reg||1
Z||000014||revin||11-26-2001||02:09 PM||||run sets of lights out to the car in front, can't untangle the string?? just put them in a big pitcher or a large jar.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Cheever3000||11-26-2001||07:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>my favorite decoration is dark blue christmas lights everywhere - looks awesome at night - esp when there is snow all around<BR> <BR> just have to worry about you house being mistaken for a runway by passing jetliners :c)</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>I do love blue lights, but my wife can't stand them.  She says blue traditionally has nothing to do with Christmas.  I'm like, so?  They're beautiful!  Goes great with smooth jazz.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||1
